SUMMARY:Name That Tune (The Very Best of 7 Decades) 
DESCRIPTION:Try New Things in Toronto!\nHello everyone\,\n\nCome join us f
 or a fun day of **Name That Tune** as we travel through seven decades of u
 nforgettable songs!\n\nFrom old favourites and classic hits to songs you m
 ay not have heard in years\, we’ll put our musical memories to the test 
 while enjoying a relaxed day of laughs\, drinks\, food and good company.\n
 \n\\*Please note that we are at The Pheasant: A Firkin Pub at 1999 Avenue 
 Road (roughly 6 blocks north of Lawrence and south of the 401). We are in 
 the back dining area—come find us!\n\n\\*Joined by my other groups too :
 )\n\nEvent details below:\n\nSincerely\,\n\nSteve Flemming\n(Organizer/Hos
 t)\n──────────────\nEvent details\n**Name That
  Tune – The Very Best of 7 Decades!**\n\\*You will be in groups of 4 to 
 6 people (working as a team)\n• Music spanning seven decades\n• Classi
 c hits and memorable favourites from different eras\n• Meet new people a
 nd reconnect with familiar faces\n─────────────
 ─\nFriendly reminders\nEvent fee: $10 per person for reserved seating an
 d event organization.\nFood and drinks are purchased separately.\nPay the 
 event fee in cash at the event or by e-transfer in advance to:\n[steveflem
 ming11@gmail.com](mailto:steveflemming11@gmail.com)\n\\*Great dinner menu 
 and food specials provided\n\\*One beverage or appetizer minimum upon arri
 val to support the venue\n──────────────\nPark
 ing and transportation\n\\*Lots of street parking on Avenue Road and free 
 residential parking\nThe Pheasant: A Firkin Pub:\n[https://www.firkinpubs.
 com/thepheasantandfirkin/](https://www.firkinpubs.com/thepheasantandfirkin
 /)\n\\*15–20 minute walk from Yonge & Lawrence subway station—or simpl
 y take the bus or an Uber from the station.
