SUMMARY:Music Appreciation from the 1950s\, 1960s and 1970s Social Event! 
DESCRIPTION:Try New Things in Toronto!\nGood day everyone\,\n\nJoin us for
  a fun and interactive Sunday night celebrating the music of the **’50s\
 , ’60s and ’70s**! We’ll listen to great songs from all three decade
 s\, share memories and talk about the artists and sounds that made each er
 a memorable.\nㅤ\n\n* **The ’50s** brought us early rock ’n’ roll\,
  rockabilly and doo-wop\, with artists like Elvis Presley\, Chuck Berry an
 d Buddy Holly.\n* **The ’60s** gave us the Beatles\, the Beach Boys and 
 the Supremes\, along with the sounds of the British Invasion\, surf pop an
 d Motown.\n* **The ’70s** took us from Gordon Lightfoot and Fleetwood Ma
 c to Stevie Wonder and the Bee Gees\, with singer-songwriters\, classic ro
 ck\, soul and disco.\n\nㅤ\nWhether you grew up with these songs or disco
 vered them years later\, everyone is encouraged to join in. Bring a favour
 ite song or album to talk about\, share a memory\, or come hear a few forg
 otten gems and meet other people who love music.\nㅤ\n*We’ll be joined 
 by my other social groups too\, so we can look forward to a friendly crowd
  and good conversation!*\nㅤ\n*We’ll be in the back dining area at The 
 Pheasant: A Firkin Pub\, 1999 Avenue Road\, roughly six blocks north of La
 wrence Avenue and south of the 401. When you arrive\, ask the bartender or
  wait staff for Steve’s event.*\nㅤ\nSincerely\,\nSteve Flemming\n(Orga
 nizer/Host)\nㅤ\n\n***\n\n### Event Details\n\n**About Your Host**\nSteve
  Flemming has been a DJ since the early 2000s and has a lifelong passion f
 or music\, especially from the 1960s through the 1990s. His father was als
 o a DJ during the ’70s and ’80s\, so music was a big part of Steve’s
  life growing up. He enjoys sharing great songs and bringing people togeth
 er through music.\nㅤ\n**Event Fee**\n**$5 per person** (HST included). P
 ay cash at the door or send an e-transfer to [steveflemming11@gmail.com](m
 ailto:steveflemming11@gmail.com).\n*No extra charge for those attending th
 e earlier event.*\nㅤ\n**Friendly Reminders**\n\n* Please arrive anytime 
 between **6:00 p.m. and 8:00 p.m.**\, if possible.\n* You’re welcome to 
 arrive earlier. Please ask for Steve when you arrive.\n* The Pheasant offe
 rs a dinner menu and food specials.\n* To help support the venue\, please 
 purchase at least one beverage or appetizer upon arrival.\n\nㅤ\n**Parkin
 g and Transportation**\nThere’s street parking along Avenue Road and fre
 e parking on nearby residential side streets where permitted.\nㅤ\nThe ve
 nue is approximately a 15–20-minute walk from Lawrence subway station at
  Yonge and Lawrence. You can also take a bus or Uber from the station.\n
 ㅤ\n[The Pheasant: A Firkin Pub website](https://www.firkinpubs.com/theph
 easantandfirkin/)
